WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.042
This query partitions employees by department and orders salary descending.

00:00:05.042 --> 00:00:08.337
RANK restarts at one for each department.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:12.277
Run the query and notice the boundaries between departments.

00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:18.912
This is a common pattern for top earners, top products, or highest values within categories.

00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:23.977
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:23.977 --> 00:00:30.327
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:30.327 --> 00:00:32.737
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:37.882
In a real setting such as a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions,

00:00:37.882 --> 00:00:43.887
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:43.887 --> 00:00:46.357
before discussing syntax.

00:00:46.357 --> 00:00:52.880
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
